  "id": "group",
  "term": "group",
  "definition": "A group is a set of individuals taken together while still being recognized as distinct from one another. In this historical psychological sense, a group differs from a general concept because it includes the particular members themselves rather than an abstract common quality, and it may be concrete or more abstract and numerical.",
